entally punch my microphone and I  apologize for that I know it's a much  bigger deal to people listening than it  is to me here in the room the number of  unauthorized immigrants arriving in the  u.s. reached more than 800,000 annually  between 2000 and 2005 however after 2007  the  number of undocumented immigrants coming  into the u.s. has dropped drastically  we've seen also at this point that we  are seeing about the same number of  undocumented immigrants 400,000 leave  every year as the number that comes back  and you will often not hear that we hear  just about the inflow net though we at  this point do not seem to be  experiencing an increase in the number  of undocumented immigrants coming into  the country we have so many issues that  are just way way bigger than this the  the idea that we are going to focus on  this issue I am not advocating for  people to break the law by coming into  this country illegally you know that I  don't do that but think for a second  about the real problems that we have the  banking crisis of 2008 nothing to do  with legal or undocumented immigrants  the constant war industrial complex  including middle-east wars not caused by  immigrants if anything it contributes to  the refugee situation that we find  ourselves in the explosive growth and  income and wealth inequality combined  with the effective oligarchy that we  have in our country and the  disproportionate power of huge  corporations not caused by immigrants  the fact that health insurance is a  for-profit commodity to be bought and  sold that has nothing to do with  immigrants what this is really about is  something very common which is it's  about figuring out who you can blame  right across the last I don't know 2000  years in much of the world it's been a  lot of blame the Jews stuff immigrants  are now taking up some of that in the  United States but really it is code for  Hispanic and Muslim immigrants not  actually all immigrants and it is really  really effective especially politically  to have someone to nicely and neatly  blame for problems and sadly to too many  people it doesn't matter what some study  says by some legitimate agency many  people feel like immigrants are taking  their jobs and that's really what  matters many of our viewers and  listeners know that just posting your  job listing on one website isn't enough  to find quality candidates if you want  to find  perfect hire you really need to post  your job on all the top job sites and  now you can with zip recruiter dot-com  you can post your job to 100 plus job  sites including social media networks  like Facebook and Twitter all with a  single click you can find candidates in  any city any industry nationwide just  post once and watch your qualified  candidates roll into zip recruiters easy  to use interface no juggling emails no  juggling calls to your office you can  quickly screen candidates rate them and  hire the right person quickly find out  today why zip recruiter has been used by  over a million businesses and right now  david pakman show listeners can post  jobs on zip recruiter for free by going  to zip recruiter dot-com slash free  trial that is zip recruiter dot-com  slash free trial one more time try it  for free at zip recruiter dot-com slash  free trial
 

